# UI Conventions

- Prefer `PageHeader`, `EmptyState`, and helpers from `page-primitives.tsx` over one-off page chrome.
- Compose shadcn primitives from `components/ui/` inside feature folders (`findings/`, `dashboard/`, `requirements/`).
- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when interactivity requires it.
- Meet the same accessibility bar we enforce on scanned apps: labels, keyboard access, semantic HTML (jsx-a11y is strict).
- Use domain vocabulary in UI copy (Finding, Requirement, Remediation) — not "issue" or "violation" in chrome.
- Status UI: reuse existing badges/tokens; surface automated vs `human_review` when the status source matters.
